# SE4-P6: byte copy of ge-proton11-12-se4-p4.env with only PIN_ID and PIN_BUILD_NAME changed (and this line). Series patches/series-ge-proton11-12-se4-p6 = SE4-P4 + 0046 (mfmediaengine: never call the application with the engine lock held) + 0048 (mf: never hold the audio renderer lock across audio driver calls).
# SE4-P4: byte copy of ge-proton11-12-se4-p3.env with PIN_ID, PIN_BUILD_NAME and the two PIN_FFMPEG_HLS_INIT_CONFIG_* lines changed or added (and this line). Wine series = SE4-P3's; FFmpeg adds companion E6 (hls.c: announce a changed init section's codec configuration).
# SE4-P3: byte copy of ge-proton11-12-se4-p2.env with only PIN_ID and PIN_BUILD_NAME changed (and this line). Series patches/series-ge-proton11-12-se4-p3 = SE4-P2 + 0044 (live-HLS discontinuity timeline).
# SE4-P2: byte copy of ge-proton11-12-se4-p1-r2.env with only PIN_ID and PIN_BUILD_NAME changed (and this line). Series patches/series-ge-proton11-12-se4-p2 = SE4-P1 + 0043 (F1).
# SE4-P1 r2: the draft pin plus a second GE deviation. GE-Proton11-12's protonfixes patch 0003 (Kingdoms of Amalur gamefix) re-creates two files
# that the pinned protonfixes 28a02c25 already contains byte-identically, which stops the fail-fast driver; r2 skips it (a no-op against GE's effective build). Build name unchanged.
# SE4-P1 draft: GE-Proton11-12 + a reworked project Wine series + the existing FFmpeg modules + the HTTP chunked-end module.
# Series: patches/series-ge-proton11-12-se4-p1 (patch files in patches/ge-proton11-12-se4-p1/); not final when this pin was written.
# The pin does not bind the series; verify-preparation binds its digest per pin.
# FFmpeg: unchanged gitlink 9047fa1b; the four security backports, secure-RTSP, HTTP-seek, HTTP-filesize, HTTP chunked-end
# (new in SE4-P1), HLS early-seek, crypto/MPEG-video/AAC-parser build modules. The three build modules patch GE's root
# Makefile.in, which changed in GE-Proton11-12, so their final Makefile.in blobs differ from SE3's.
# Deviation from GE: the prepared GE driver copy omits GE's post-series rtworkq hotfix
# (patches/wine-hotfixes/pending/rtworkq-dont-hold-queues-section-during-system-queue-shutdown.patch, GE issue 899).
# The project series carries its own rtworkq patch 0025, which also closes a startup-during-shutdown race that GE's hotfix leaves open;
# the two conflict. See PIN_GE_SKIP_PATCHES below.
# Inputs: new GE tag/commit/tree, Wine fda79a58, moved gitlinks (FEX, d7vk, dxvk, dxvk-nvapi, protonfixes, vkd3d, vkd3d-proton);
# driver and root Makefile.in blobs changed; Wine-Staging, .gitmodules, configure.sh, rules-meson.mk unchanged.
# Contrib: Xalia 0.5.0.1 (new). Media cleanup: re-bound to GE-Proton11-12's trimmed video-removal patch 0001.
# Fresh source: worktrees/ge-proton11-12-se4-p1-rtsp
# Fresh state: work/ge-proton11-12-se4-p1; build path chosen explicitly at build time.
# Default schedule: Make 4 x Ninja 2; PACKAGE_RELEASE remains zero.

